<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia hikes internal coffee price to new high.</title>
<headline>Colombia hikes internal coffee price to new high.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia raised its internal coffe price to a new high of 383,375 pesos per 125-kg load Friday in the sixth such increase since Jan. 31, the National Coffee Growers' Federation said.</p>
<p>It said the increase marked a 6.79 percent rise from the price set last Friday, when the 125-kg load was valued at 359,000 pesos.</p>
<p>The new price, which should hold for at least 10 days, was based on average Colombian coffee prices in New York over the past week of $2.26 per pound, the federation said. Colombia's internal coffee price has shot up by nearly 69 percent since the start of the year as authorities move to bring it closer into line with world market prices.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
